  "question": {
    "text": "The effect of increase in temperature on the number of electrons in conduction band $\\left(\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{e}}\\right)$ and resistance of a semiconductor will be as:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Both $\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{e}}$ and resistance decrease",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Both $\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{e}}$ and resistance increase",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{e}}$ increases, resistance decreases",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$n_e$ decreases, resistance increases",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "When temperature increases, more electrons excite to conduction band and hence conductivity increases, therefore resistance decreases."
  }
